        "title": "refactor: remove browser and codex dead exports",
        "body": "Related: #105595\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nRemoves every remaining unused production export from the browser and Codex plugins so the shrink-only dead-export ratchet reflects code that is actually reachable in production. The original cluster contained 555 scoped findings; current `main` absorbed 39 overlapping removals while this PR was in progress.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBrowser Playwright helpers now use one canonical export path instead of duplicate re-export chains. Other dead plugin exports and tests that existed only to cover them were deleted; Codex protocol-shaped surfaces were checked against the sibling Codex source, while plugin entry barrels and canonical protocol namespaces remain intact.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Against current `main`, the dead-export baseline falls from 5,526 to 5,010 entries (516 net), with zero browser or Codex findings.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports:update` regenerated the pushed baseline immediately before push; `pnpm deadcode:exports` passes with 5,010 entries and zero browser or Codex findings.\n- The final rebase absorbed main's concurrent path-safety cleanup; the exact current-main comparison remains shrink-only by 516 entries.\n- Browser suite: 138 files, 1,796 passed, 1 skipped; final CDP fixture rerun: 43 passed.\n- Codex suite: 106 files, 2,486 passed; final command-handler rerun: 148 passed.\n- `pnpm check:architecture` passes, including zero runtime import cycles and zero Madge cycles.\n- `pnpm check:test-types`: core, extensions, and root test typechecks passed.\n- Changed-surface format, SDK baseline, package guards, typechecks, core lint, and focused extension lint passed; four stale test imports found during the gate were removed and their 35-test rerun passed.\n- Fresh Codex autoreviews across the large change, rebase conflict resolution, and final CI-gate fix reported no remaining actionable findings.\n",
